Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Observability Pods Not Starting
Symptoms: Pods in open-cluster-management-observability namespace are in Pending or CrashLoopBackOff state.

Solution:

# Check pod events
oc describe pod <pod-name> -n open-cluster-management-observability

# Check resource availability
oc describe nodes | grep -A 5 "Allocated resources"

# Restart the observability operator
oc rollout restart deployment/multicluster-observability-operator -n open-cluster-management
Issue 2: Metrics Not Appearing in Grafana
Symptoms: Dashboards show "No data" or empty graphs.

Solution:

# Verify Prometheus targets
oc exec -n open-cluster-management-observability deployment/observability-thanos-query -- \
  curl -s "http://localhost:9090/api/v1/targets" | jq '.data.activeTargets[] | select(.health != "up")'

# Check ServiceMonitor configuration
oc get servicemonitors -n open-cluster-management-observability -o yaml

# Verify network connectivity
oc exec -n open-cluster-management-observability deployment/observability-grafana -- \
  curl -s "http://observability-thanos-query:9090/api/v1/query?query=up"
Issue 3: Alerts Not Firing
Symptoms: Expected alerts are not showing up in AlertManager.

Solution:

# Check PrometheusRule syntax
oc get prometheusrules cluster-health-alerts -n open-cluster-management-observability -o yaml

# Verify alert evaluation
oc exec -n open-cluster-management-observability deployment/observability-thanos-query -- \
  curl -s "http://localhost:9090/api/v1/rules" | jq '.data.groups[] | select(.name=="cluster.health")'

# Check AlertManager configuration
oc get secret alertmanager-main -n open-cluster-management-observability -o jsonpath='{.data.alertmanager\.yaml}' | base64 -d
